1
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:07,554
Every December, new starters and remote colleagues need a holiday

2
00:00:07,554 --> 00:00:12,310
sweater, while the shared cupboard turns into an unwashed free-for-all.

3
00:00:12,760 --> 00:00:18,444
Loan Chest puts the whole wardrobe in a tall wooden chest of drawers: brass

4
00:00:18,444 --> 00:00:23,370
tags show code and size, and each folded knit peeks over the lip.

5
00:00:23,820 --> 00:00:28,438
Drawers slide out as loans progress; overdue drawers pull askew in amber,

6
00:00:28,438 --> 00:00:32,170
and garments in the two-day cleaning gap carry a steam tag.

7
00:00:33,106 --> 00:00:37,496
Switch to the Wear lens and click the Today alert for LC-03.

8
00:00:37,946 --> 00:00:42,566
At eleven of twelve wears, its next return will retire the sweater automatically.

9
00:00:43,370 --> 00:00:46,819
Flip View As to Borrower and every drawer that fits your

10
00:00:46,819 --> 00:00:51,130
chest measurement within zero to twenty centimetres of ease lights up.

11
00:00:51,931 --> 00:00:56,626
When three colleagues want the same sweater, the Waiting list ranks

12
00:00:56,626 --> 00:01:01,111
by days since last loan—so a never-borrowed newcomer wins first.

13
00:01:01,912 --> 00:01:06,082
On the Return slip, a three-day overdue loan logs a two-dollar

14
00:01:06,082 --> 00:01:11,732
charity-jar donation after the one-day grace period, without ever blocking check-in.

15
00:01:12,182 --> 00:01:16,992
Checking in LC-03 records its twelfth wear and retires it from the chest.
